speechtext:
There are some of the smaller amounts that I think would be for repairs, but all the larger amounts are
for new construction. Mather's island, Chase wharf, Chase's point. Oromocto, McGowan, Sheffield and Rothesay, are all new. Rothesay was the wharf that was purchased from the Almon estate and rebuilt. Burton court house, Barker's,

Jemseg and Scotchtown, are all new. A very large number of them are new works.

1.	What amount of money or its equivalent was in the hands or control of the Quebec Bridge Company at the time of the collapse of the Quebec bridge?
2.	What became of the money';
3.	Was any of the money paid to the directors of the company? If so, what sums, to whom and on what account?
